---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Work with me"
  description="Four ways to work with Ryan Laird: strategic communications, mentoring, teaching and tutoring, and speaking, media or research collaboration."
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="sl">Work with me</p>

      <h1>Four routes, one for what you need</h1>

      <p class="lede">
        I work with organisations, students, professionals and event hosts. They need different things, so the routes
        below are separate. Choose the one that fits and you’ll land on the right page.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="route-grid">
      <article class="route" id="consulting" data-tone="teal">
        <h2>Strategic communications and advisory</h2>
        <p>Positioning, content and digital strategy for organisations working with technical, scientific or environmental subject matter.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> space, Earth observation, climate and sustainability organisations; science and technology businesses; mission-led and public-interest initiatives.</p>
        <p class="for">Organisation-level projects are delivered through Green Orbit Digital.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/consulting/">How consulting works</a>
      </article>

      <article class="route" id="teaching-and-mentoring" data-tone="violet">
        <h2>Mentoring</h2>
        <p>Structured one-to-one conversations about career direction, moving between science and communications, and working in mission-led fields.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> early- and mid-career professionals, and scientists considering communications, policy, engagement or commercial roles.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/mentoring/">How mentoring works</a>
        <a class="go" href="/coaching/">ADHD-informed coaching</a>
      </article>

      <article class="route" data-tone="sky">
        <h2>Teaching, tutoring and workshops</h2>
        <p>Physics and astronomy tutoring, guest lectures, and workshops on communicating complex topics.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> students, adult learners, schools, universities, charities, networks and professional teams.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/teaching/">Tutoring, talks and workshops</a>
        <a class="go" href="/tutoring/">Physics and astronomy tuition (GCSE and A-level)</a>
      </article>

      <article class="route" id="speaking" data-tone="amber">
        <h2>Speaking, media and collaboration</h2>
        <p>Talks, panels, podcast and press contributions, and research or editorial collaborations.</p>
        <p class="for"><strong>For:</strong> conference and event organisers, podcast hosts, journalists and editors, universities and public-engagement teams, research collaborators.</p>
        <a class="go" href="/press/">Press kit and past appearances</a>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="block">
      <h2>Not sure which route fits?</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, pick the closest option and describe what you have in mind. If it
        belongs with another route, or with Green Orbit Digital, I’ll say so.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>